<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK APRIL M2 UP 14.9 PCT YR/YR (+21.2 PCT).</title>
<headline>SLOVAK APRIL M2 UP 14.9 PCT YR/YR (+21.2 PCT).</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The key Slovak money supply</p>
<p>aggregate, M2, rose 14.9 percent year-on-year in April,</p>
<p>compared with a 12-month increase of 21.2 percent in April</p>
<p>1996, the National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said in its April</p>
<p>monetary survey obtained by Reuters on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The M2 rose by 12.8 percent year-on-year in March 1997.</p>
<p>SLOVAK MONEY SUPPLY  APRIL 97  MAR 97  FEB 97  APRIL 96  FY 96</p>
<p> M2 overall (SKK bln)  411.2     408.1   406.5   358.0    416.9</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	+14.9     +12.8   +13.9   +21.2     15.7</p>
<p>Note. All figures are subject to revision. The NBS's</p>
<p>full-year target for M2 expansion is 10.7 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>M2 measures currency, demand and time deposits, savings</p>
<p>deposits and foreign currency deposits.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-521-8402</p>
